      "problem": "What is the center of the hyperbola $\\frac{(y-1)^{2}}{16}-\\frac{(x-3)^{2}}{4}=1?$",
      "worked_solution": "The equation of a vertical hyperbola centered at $(h,k)$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{(y-k)^{2}}{{a}^{2}}-\\frac{(x-h)^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\nIn this case, we have $h=3$ and $k=1.$\n\nTherefore, the center of the hyperbola is $(3,1).$",
